  "version": "as-filed",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id)\n(section) Sec. 758 (as in the version read)\n(quote) (g) Applies for an absent voter ballot in person with the clerk of the township, city, or village in which he or she is registered, and he or she identifies himself or herself to the clerk by presenting an official state personal identification card issued to that elector under 1972 PA 222, MCL 28.291 to 28.300, an operator's or chauffeur's license issued to that elector under the Michigan vehicle code, 1949 PA 300, MCL 257.1 to 257.923, or another generally recognized picture identification card.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule) not stated.\n(other) Sec. 759: begins \"(1) At any time during the 75 days before a primary or special primary, but not later than 2 p.m. of the Saturday immediately befo\"",
